# English screen corpus for iomoont (the PRESS START tournament MOD), at the
# Netherlands country default (SW40-2/3/4 = country 4, English text, F11).
# No DIP override is set: the DEFAULT in SLEIC2_COMPORTS already selects it.
#
# Two games, then the service-menu tree. Game 1 is the original feature-
# coverage game (both ramps, the orbit lane, all five bumpers twice round,
# both bull's-eyes, the drop bank walked to 2/4/5 targets, the inner bank,
# both holes, Jupiter's lock twice for multiball, two tilt warnings to a
# full tilt -- tilt warns defaults to 1, F10) at an ordinary, non-
# qualifying score, ending at the mod's own PRESS START screen at the
# normal end-of-game hook (D5123) -- unchanged from the previously
# committed script (same labels, same relative timing), so every existing
# citation of those exact labels stays valid against this capture. Game 2
# is a fresh credit and a second three-ball game (labels prefixed
# "score-") played purely to clear the high-score bar and walk the
# initials wheel: three balls of unlit-lane hits (100,000 each, docs/
# iomoon_game_rules.md 3.3.1/5.6) put the score around 233,000,000, well
# above the lowest fresh-NVRAM high-score preset (50,000,000 at NVRAM
# 0x85, F10) with margin to spare, then the awarded extra ball is drained
# for real (five diverse hits, not a bare plunge), then the RECORD
# INSCRIPTION screen is walked with the flippers and fixed with START.
# Then the whole 38-record service-menu tree (SOUND/VIDEO, GAME,
# TECHNICAL -- F14).
#
# Keys: L/R Ctrl + R/H/B qualify Ramp, Hole, Bull Eye 1 vs 2; W/E/D/F/G are
# Bumpers 1-5; J Jupiter; I Inner Bank; O Lane 10 (orbit); K Lane 11;
# Z/X/C/V/N Drop targets A-E; Y/U/A/S/M/L/,/./ Lanes 1-9; Q Drain; Space
# plunges; Down follows the next ball after a drain (src/wpc/sims/sleic/
# iomoon.c). 1/5/7/T are START/COIN/TEST/TILT (sleic.h SLEIC_CABPORT); on
# the high-score entry screen and in the service menu alike, the left/right
# flipper keys (LShift/RShift) move backward/forward and START fixes/
# selects; in the service menu specifically, BOTH START and TEST back up
# exactly one level from wherever the cursor is (F14's "redraw, return 1"
# for TEST and "sub_DF829" for START are the same one-pop action, not two
# different ones) -- "exit the whole menu, reboot the Z80" is not a
# separate action, it is just what backing up from record 0 (root)
# necessarily does, since root has no parent. One case does not fit this:
# backing out of an auto-cycling test (SOLENOIDS, the three LIGHT TESTs,
# the three CONTACTOS-adjacent tests) with TEST can land straight at
# record 0 with the menu still open rather than at its immediate parent.
# The walk below always follows a leaf back up with as many single pops as
# its own depth (ordinary records) or, for an auto-cycling test, treats
# whatever TEST lands on next as unknown and re-settles from there rather
# than assuming one pop -- and a final, explicit TEST-from-root closes the
# menu for real at the very end, checked by confirming the tail of the
# dump is live attract animation, not a static frame.
#
# What fix round 3 settled, against F10/F11: F10/F11's short-ball "salida
# nula" replay protection (sub_D368C, NVRAM 0x43, factory threshold
# 100,000) replays any ball -- an awarded extra ball included -- that
# scores at or below the threshold, indistinguishable from an abandoned
# ball; a bare plunge-and-drain scores exactly zero and loops forever.
# That is not specific to extra balls and is not a fault in the ball
# simulator: the recovery ball below is given five diverse real hits (a
# bumper, a bull's-eye, a drop target, a ramp, Jupiter) before it drains,
# which clears the floor easily and lets the game end for real. With that
# fixed, both the qualifying score and the RECORD INSCRIPTION screen are
# reached cleanly, and the wheel-walk below shows the selected character
# changing at every single marked step (confirmed against the h=12 face,
# now pinned at table offset 75: the decoded "PLAYER 1 : ..." tail grows
# and changes at every mark, e.g. ... -> D -> G -> M -> ... -> fixed) --
# not a static screen with the key presses merely passed through. One
# LEFT-flipper step from a fresh character slot lands on a position the
# h=12 face cannot read as a letter (unlike every surrounding step),
# consistent with the "<-" erase symbol (docs/iomoon_game_rules.md 4.2);
# START on it is exercised as the erase demonstration.
#
# The wheel-walk's own timing turned out to be exact-frame sensitive: an
# extra, otherwise harmless 300-frame gap between the recovery ball's
# drain and the high-score-entry mark (a leftover from drafting against
# the mod's ordinary, non-qualifying end-of-game screen) was enough by
# itself to make the entry screen revert to plain PRESS START partway
# through the wheel-walk, with no other change to the recipe. Removing
# that one gap (the drain's own settle flows straight into the entry
# screen) fixed it outright, confirmed against both a short and the full,
# multi-thousand-frame attract wait used below -- so it was that specific
# timing artifact, not the game's position in the session or the feature
# hits in the other game.
#
# The mod's SPECIAL trampoline (D5077, the match-win path) is still not
# exercised. The qualifying score and the RECORD INSCRIPTION screen are
# both reached cleanly now (above), which was the blocker fix rounds 1-2
# recorded; what replaces it is that no distinct match/lottery screen was
# found at all in the window after either the qualifying game above or an
# ordinary, non-qualifying one -- both go straight from PRESS START back
# into the normal attract cycle (checked directly against the current
# h=12 decoder, which reads the attract ad screens fine, and against the
# raw dump, which shows only ordinary attract content, not a match digit
# or a third distinct PRESS START). Reaching D5077 needs an actual match
# win, which this walk does not force. See dmd/README.md and the task
# report for what was tried.
#
# Fix round 5: the service-menu tree's own record-to-record dwell (the gap
# between a "mark svc-N" and the tap that advances to the next record) was
# stretched from ~120 frames to 3000 for every ordinary single-hop
# transition, on the theory that a deeper record's item text was still
# settling when the walk advanced past it -- a scene's representative is
# whatever stands last before the next mark, so a longer window should
# show a still-settling page as done. It mostly did not: root and record 1
# were already correct and stay that way; of the other 36 records, only
# svc-35 (an auto-cycling LIGHT TEST record) gained real content (one
# legible LIGHT: LCn readout) that the shorter dwell had not caught. The
# other deep records decode the identical h=12 tile-bar pattern at 3000
# frames that they did at ~120, which points at that pattern being the
# stable drawn state at this depth rather than a transition a longer wait
# would resolve -- see dmd/README.md and the task report's "Fix round 5"
# section for the measurement. The larger transitions this walk already
# uses for back-out-and-reopen sequences (240-1200 frames, and the
# 5200-frame menu-reopen wait) are untouched: an earlier attempt that also
# stretched those desynced the auto-cycling-test navigation and landed the
# walk in ordinary attract mid-menu, so only the plain 120-frame hops were
# touched here.
